{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>He cast into the sea.</b> 'שְׁדִי בְיַמָּא' — שְׁדִי is a term of casting. And so it says ״אוֹ יָרֹה יִיָּרֶה״ (Exodus 19) — אוֹ אִשְׁתְּדָאָה יִשְׁתְּדִי, and the tav serves in these forms in place of the hitpa'el (reflexive stem)." "<b>And the choice.</b> A noun. Like מֶרְכָּב, מִשְׁכָּב, מִקְרָא קֹדֶשׁ." "<b>They sank.</b> טְבִיעָה is only in a place of mud, like ״טָבַעְתִּי בִּיוֵן מְצוּלָה״ (Psalms 69), ״וַיִּטְבַּע יִרְמְיָהוּ בַּטִּיט״ (Jeremiah 38) — this teaches that the sea became mud, to requite them measure for measure, that they enslaved Israel with mortar and bricks (Mekhilta)."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:52:20.300330909Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}